      "side": 1,
      "message": "From your explanation sounds like trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_reset_wmark() does not necessarily reset the watermark but readjusts it. But even then it sounds like you might end up exiting __alloc_pages_slowpath() without calling trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_reset_wmark() and without restoring the watermark. Is that your intention? If not, are you perhaps using trace_android_vh_alloc_pages_slowpath_end() to restore the watermark to its original value?\n\nOverall naming these hooks trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_reset_wmark() and trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_adjust_wmark() is confusing. I suggest renaming trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_adjust_wmark() to trace_android_vh_alloc_pages_reclaim_start() since it\u0027s called at the start of the direct reclaim. trace_android_rvh_alloc_pages_reset_wmark() I would name trace_android_vh_alloc_pages_reclaim_cycle_end() because it\u0027s called at the end of a reclaim cycle.",
